{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He shall bring him.</b> The Sages of blessed memory already explained that he brings himself. This is because indeed, whoever draws near to one who effects something upon him is said to be brought to the one acting upon him by means of one more honored than himself — as when a prisoner does not release himself. Therefore it was written concerning the metzora, both in his impurity and in his purification, וְהוּבָא אֶל הַכֹּהֵן (Leviticus 14:2), and concerning the sotah, וְהֵבִיא הָאִישׁ אֶת אִשְׁתּוֹ אֶל הַכֹּהֵן (Numbers 5:15), and likewise concerning the slave, וְהִגִּישׁוֹ אֲדֹנָיו אֶל הָאֱלֹהִים (Exodus 21:6). But in the case of the nazirite, upon whom the shaving is effected and through whom he is transformed into a different man, there is none more honored than himself to bring him — rather, he brings himself."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:51.792437360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}